Show the WiFi password dialog even when gnome-keyring is not installed.

GNOME Shell's NM secret agent queries org.freedesktop.secrets before
prompting and aborts the request (NM_SECRET_AGENT_ERROR_FAILED, no dialog)
when the service is missing. GNOME 48 added the force-always-ask property
(commit 65d38939, MR !3646) which skips the keyring lookup and prompts
directly, but only enables it in greeter mode. Enable it unconditionally:
NetworkManager saves WPA-PSK secrets system-owned (psk-flags=0) in
/etc/NetworkManager/system-connections by itself, so no keyring is needed
to prompt, save or reconnect. Only agent-owned ("this user only") secrets
lose keyring lookup, which cannot work without a keyring anyway.

--- a/js/ui/components/networkAgent.js	2026-07-03 12:21:49.393054289 +0200
+++ b/js/ui/components/networkAgent.js	2026-07-03 12:21:49.396054289 +0200
@@ -676,7 +676,7 @@
             identifier: 'org.gnome.Shell.NetworkAgent',
             capabilities: NM.SecretAgentCapabilities.VPN_HINTS,
             auto_register: false,
-            force_always_ask: Main.sessionMode.isGreeter,
+            force_always_ask: true,
         });
 
         this._dialogs = { };
